{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Elohim blessed them, saying</b> — He decreed the blessing upon them and said of them that they should be fruitful and multiply, that is, that they should produce many fruits, so that one brings forth many like itself. The concept of blessing pertains to bringing forth offspring, as in what He said: And I will bless her, and she shall become nations (Genesis 17:16). And also in the case of plants the language of blessing occurs: (Leviticus 25:21), and I will command My blessing for you in the sixth year. But this was not said on the third day, because the created beings among all creatures with a living soul were only two in number, male and female according to their kind, as in the case of man, and they needed a blessing to multiply greatly; but the plants sprouted across the face of all the earth very many, as they are this day. And He did not state a blessing for the beasts and the wild animals, because from this very decree that He decreed upon the creatures possessing the power of movement that are in the waters — the abundance — the creatures possessing the power of movement on earth also multiplied, for all living creatures that are not speaking beings are all one matter in their creation. And our Rabbis said (Bereshit Rabbah 11:3) that because people hunt from among them and eat them, they needed a blessing." "<b>And fill the waters in the seas</b> — He blessed them that they should fill, by virtue of their abundance, the seas and also the streams and the pools; or, their filling in the seas means that in the streams they are few." "<b>And let the fowl multiply on the earth</b> — Even though its creation was from the waters, its blessing was to be on the earth, that it should be fruitful and multiply upon it, for there is no bird that lays its eggs in the water and raises them there; rather, even those that dwell continuously in the water and are nourished from it make their eggs on the earth and are born there."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-21T22:14:59.639466225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}